[{"documents":[{"i":13,"t":"Introduction","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/","b":["Installation Instructions"]},{"i":15,"t":"Installing the JDK using the Install JDK wizard","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/install-jdk-wizard","b":["Installation Instructions","Windows Installation","Installing the Java Development Kit (JDK)"]},{"i":17,"t":"Installing the Java Development Kit (JDK)","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/installing-jdk","b":["Installation Instructions","Windows Installation","Installing the Java Development Kit (JDK)"]},{"i":19,"t":"Installing the JDK from the Azul Website","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/installing-jdk-from-Azul","b":["Installation Instructions","Windows Installation","Installing the Java Development Kit (JDK)"]},{"i":21,"t":"Windows Installation","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/windows-installation","b":["Installation Instructions","Windows Installation"]},{"i":23,"t":"Installing Scripture App Builder","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/installing-scripture-app-builder","b":["Installation Instructions","Windows Installation"]}],"index":{"version":"2.3.9","fields":["t"],"fieldVectors":[["t/13",[0,2.193]],["t/15",[1,0.281,2,0.808,3,1.222,4,1.222]],["t/17",[1,0.21,2,0.603,5,1.341,6,1.341,7,1.341]],["t/19",[1,0.233,2,0.668,8,1.485,9,1.485]],["t/21",[1,0.296,10,1.892]],["t/23",[1,0.233,11,1.485,12,1.485,13,1.485]]],"invertedIndex":[["app",{"_index":12,"t":{"23":{"position":[[21,3]]}}}],["azul",{"_index":8,"t":{"19":{"position":[[28,4]]}}}],["builder",{"_index":13,"t":{"23":{"position":[[25,7]]}}}],["develop",{"_index":6,"t":{"17":{"position":[[20,11]]}}}],["instal",{"_index":1,"t":{"15":{"position":[[0,10],[29,7]]},"17":{"position":[[0,10]]},"19":{"position":[[0,10]]},"21":{"position":[[8,12]]},"23":{"position":[[0,10]]}}}],["introduct",{"_index":0,"t":{"13":{"position":[[0,12]]}}}],["java",{"_index":5,"t":{"17":{"position":[[15,4]]}}}],["jdk",{"_index":2,"t":{"15":{"position":[[15,3],[37,3]]},"17":{"position":[[36,5]]},"19":{"position":[[15,3]]}}}],["kit",{"_index":7,"t":{"17":{"position":[[32,3]]}}}],["scriptur",{"_index":11,"t":{"23":{"position":[[11,9]]}}}],["us",{"_index":3,"t":{"15":{"position":[[19,5]]}}}],["websit",{"_index":9,"t":{"19":{"position":[[33,7]]}}}],["window",{"_index":10,"t":{"21":{"position":[[0,7]]}}}],["wizard",{"_index":4,"t":{"15":{"position":[[41,6]]}}}]],"pipeline":["stemmer"]}},{"documents":[],"index":{"version":"2.3.9","fields":["t"],"fieldVectors":[],"invertedIndex":[],"pipeline":["stemmer"]}},{"documents":[{"i":14,"t":"Scripture App Builder does what its name suggests: it helps you to build customized Scripture apps for smartphones and tablets. You specify the Scripture files to use, the app name, the fonts, the colours, the about box information, the audio and the icons. Scripture App Builder will package everything together and build the customized app for you. You then install it on your mobile device, send it to others by Bluetooth or Wi-Fi transfer app, share it on microSD memory cards and publish it to app stores on the Internet. Image To install Scripture App Builder on Windows, please follow the instructions in section 2. For Linux, please find the instructions in section 3. For Mac, you can find the installation instructions in the document Installing and Building Apps on a Mac.","s":"Introduction","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/","h":"","p":13},{"i":16,"t":"The easiest way to install the Java Development Kit (JDK) is to use the Install JDK wizard within Scripture App Builder: Launch Scripture App Builder. Click the Install JDK button on the welcome page (or select Tools → Install JDK from the main menu). Follow the instructions in the wizard to download and install the JDK. If the JDK was installed successfully, skip section 2.2.2 and go to section 2.3 to install the Android SDK.","s":"Installing the JDK using the Install JDK wizard","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/install-jdk-wizard","h":"","p":15},{"i":18,"t":"You will need version 17 of the Java Development Kit (JDK) to build apps. There are two ways of installing it: Use the Install JDK wizard within Scripture App Builder (see section 2.2.1), or Download the JDK setup file from the Azul website and run the installer (see section 2.2.2).","s":"Installing the Java Development Kit (JDK)","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/installing-jdk","h":"","p":17},{"i":20,"t":"We recommend you use Zulu, which is a free distribution of OpenJDK from Azul. Go to the Download Zulu Builds of OpenJDK website: https://www.azul.com/downloads/?version=java-17-lts&os=windows&architecture=x86-64-bit&package=jdk#zulu There are many downloads on this page, but the above link will filter the ones you see (Java Version: Java 17 LTS; Operating System: Windows; Architecture: x86 64-bit; Java Package: JDK). Scroll down the page until you see the downloads: Image You have a choice between a zip file and an msi file. Download the .msi file since it comes with its own installer program. The file you download will have a filename something like this: **zulu17.44.15-ca-jdk17.0.8-win_x64.msi** Double-click the msi file and follow the instructions in the installation wizard to install it. By default, the .msi installer will install the JDK to the following folder: C:\\Program Files\\Zulu\\zulu-17\\ info Important: If you change the JDK install folder to something other than the default folder, you will need to remember the location of the folder so you can tell Keyboard App Builder where to find the JDK.","s":"Installing the JDK from the Azul Website","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/installing-jdk-from-Azul","h":"","p":19},{"i":22,"t":"In order to run Scripture App Builder on Windows, you need to have 3 components installed on your computer: Scripture App Builder Java Development Kit (JDK) Android Software Development Kit (SDK) There is an optional fourth component to install if you want to synchronize text and audio: Aeneas audio-text synchronization tool. Here are more details on installing each of these components.","s":"Windows Installation","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/windows-installation","h":"","p":21},{"i":24,"t":"To install the Scripture App Builder program, do the following: Go to the Download page of the Scripture App Builder website: http://software.sil.org/scriptureappbuilder/download Download the latest setup program for Windows. Run the setup program, Scripture-App-Builder-x.x-Setup.exe, to install Scripture App Builder on your computer.","s":"Installing Scripture App Builder","u":"/docu-notion-sample-site/fr/installing-scripture-app-builder","h":"","p":23}],"index":{"version":"2.3.9","fields":["t"],"fieldVectors":[["t/14",[0,0.407,1,0.139,2,0.108,3,1.926,4,1.345,5,1.345,6,1.012,7,1.926,8,1.345,9,1.345,10,1.345,11,0.605,12,0.386,13,1.345,14,1.345,15,1.345,16,1.345,17,0.899,18,1.345,19,0.899,20,1.345,21,1.345,22,0.118,23,1.345,24,1.345,25,1.345,26,1.345,27,1.345,28,1.345,29,1.345,30,1.345,31,1.345,32,1.345,33,1.345,34,1.345,35,1.345,36,1.345,37,1.345,38,0.899,39,0.386,40,1.926,41,0.386,42,1.012,43,0.867,44,1.345,45,1.345,46,1.287,47,0.899,48,1.926,49,1.345]],["t/16",[0,0.343,1,0.105,2,0.105,12,0.465,22,0.141,41,0.465,42,0.729,43,0.986,50,1.62,51,1.083,52,0.465,53,0.729,54,0.729,55,0.822,56,0.986,57,1.083,58,1.62,59,1.083,60,1.62,61,1.62,62,0.729,63,1.62,64,1.083,65,1.62,66,1.62,67,1.62,68,0.465,69,1.62,70,1.62,71,1.083,72,0.729,73,1.62,74,1.083,75,1.083]],["t/18",[0,0.289,1,0.115,2,0.089,6,0.829,11,0.829,12,0.529,22,0.127,43,1.074,51,1.232,52,0.529,53,0.829,54,0.829,55,0.76,56,0.829,57,1.232,68,0.529,71,1.232,76,0.829,77,1.232,78,1.232,79,1.843,80,1.596,81,1.843,82,1.232,83,1.232,84,0.829,85,0.829]],["t/20",[1,0.055,2,0.055,6,0.512,11,1.093,12,0.326,19,0.76,22,0.123,38,0.76,39,0.326,41,0.489,42,0.512,46,0.76,52,0.586,55,0.65,56,0.512,59,0.76,62,0.767,68,0.696,72,0.512,76,0.512,77,0.76,78,1.365,80,1.139,83,0.76,84,0.512,86,1.138,87,1.704,88,1.138,89,1.138,90,1.704,91,1.138,92,1.138,93,1.704,94,1.138,95,1.138,96,1.138,97,1.138,98,1.138,99,1.138,100,1